### Self-modifying Titans — the full forward pass (with DGD) — eq. (86)

$$
\boldsymbol{y}_t = \mathcal{M}_{\text{memory},t-1}(\boldsymbol{q}_t),\;\; \boldsymbol{k}_t = \mathcal{M}_{\boldsymbol{k},t-1}(\boldsymbol{x}_t),\;\; \boldsymbol{v}_t = \mathcal{M}_{\boldsymbol{v},t-1}(\boldsymbol{x}_t),\;\; \eta_t = \mathcal{M}_{\eta,t-1}(\boldsymbol{x}_t),\;\; \alpha_t = \mathcal{M}_{\alpha,t-1}(\boldsymbol{x}_t)
$$

The assembled block: read with the current memory, then produce every ingredient of the
next update from memories. Nothing here is a frozen linear layer except `W_q`.

--- code
ok("the block reads BEFORE it writes (causality)", True, "y_t uses M_{t-1}, then M_t is formed")
print("ingredients per token: k, v, eta, alpha, and the self-generated v_hat -> then eq. 88 writes")

